://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1696106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy","html_url":"https://github.com/Vanilagy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-25T12:26:35Z","updated_at":"2024-09-25T12:47:16Z","body":"This here seems to be the code causing the divergence: (EDIT: It's not?)\r\n![CleanShot 2024-09-25 at 14 22 11](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9cd72e6-4ba4-4c8c-8e0d-a21697531f08)\r\n\r\nI think it's destructuring `owner` from the `rawRef` here, which in my case (`new A()`) is obviously undefined. Thankfully in non-prod, the code catches this returns out of the function. However, in prod it continues and then runs into an error.\r\n\r\nIs there a reason why it continues in production? Is there any scenario in which `!owner` is true and the code that follows it is still well-behaved?\r\n\r\nPerhaps this is the intended code:\r\n```js\r\n  if (!owner) {\r\n    if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== \"production\") {\r\n      warn$1(\r\n        `Missing ref owner context. ref cannot be used on hoisted vnodes. A vnode with ref must be created inside the render function.`\r\n      );\r\n    }\r\n    return;\r\n  }\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/2373944105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Vanilagy","id":1696106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTYxMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1696106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy","html_url":"https://github.com/Vanilagy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vanilagy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/2374100980","html_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/issues/12029#issuecomment-2374100980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/12029","id":2374100980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCCum186Ngef0","user":{"login":"edison1105","id":3705199,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUxOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3705199?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105","html_url":"https://github.com/edison1105","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-25T13:32:27Z","updated_at":"2024-09-25T13:38:12Z","body":"You can switch between DEV and PROD to inspect the compiled code.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b56a0fc-3847-41d1-9808-64fa6e4fdb07)\r\n\r\nAt runtime\r\n- in the DEV environment, set the ref value using `setupState[\"refName\"] = el`.\r\n- in the PROD environment, there is no `setupState` object, so the ref value is set using `ref.value = el`.\r\nHowever, `const p = new A()` is analyzed as `setup-maybe-ref`, but it is not a ref. This results in inconsistencies between DEV and PROD environments. \r\nWhile this inconsistency differs somewhat from #11373 and #4866, fundamentally, it is also a design flaw.\r\n\r\n\r\nDevelopers should follow the documentation \r\n- declare a ref to hold the element reference\r\n- useTemplateRef","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/2374100980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"edison1105","id":3705199,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUxOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3705199?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105","html_url":"https://github.com/edison1105","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/starred{/owner}{/repo}","su